hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"144","Muhammad bin Yahya and Abd al-Rahman bin Bishr bin al-Hakam told us, they said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Thabit, and Qatada On the authority of Anas, he said: Some of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked for ablution, but they did not find any, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Here is water.” I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, put his hand in the vessel containing the water, then he said: “Perform ablution in the name of God,” and I saw water bubbling from between His fingers, and the people were performing ablution, until the last of them had performed ablution. Thabit said: So I said to Anas: How old do you think they were? He said: About seventy"
